tly  about some of the specific instances  jesse gender did a wonderful video  talking about the  impact and the influence of abigail's  coming out video  but you certainly can't make bold  statements because  coming out is a incredibly personal  experience it's very different  for everyone who has to do it so rather  than  try and lump them all together and i  think  kind of do a disservice to them i  instead want to talk about something  that  i have seen start to happen in terms of  the conversations  around creators who have come out  um and something that i think  some people it would be helpful for  you to hear a certain trap that some  people are falling into  so a bit like when i talked about  elliott page this is more about the way  in which we discuss  these creators than about the creators  themselves  now if you didn't see my video on  elliott page which i'd encourage you to  do i'm not going to be re  reiterating too many of those points but  just quick reminder  uh if somebody comes out as a new  name or pronoun preference and or  gender uh you need to refer to them as  such even when you were referring to  work that they did prior to coming out  or prior to  transition public visible transition  so when you talk about abigail and  philosophy tube  it's abigail it's she even if you're  talking about work  that she did years ago while in no way  presenting as feminine  so that's basic that's basic just to  reiterate that  but instead i want to talk about  something that i tend to see  which is fans well  possibly detractors as well but anyone  who's gonna knock on a  trans or lgbtq plus or whatever  person for coming out is an audience who  isn't going to listen to me in the first  place so i'm not really going to deal  with them  but i have seen fans and people  in more or less good faith start to  become speculative  in terms of doing things like  going back through old videos looking  for early indicators  looking for signs and  starting to try and construct a timeline  of transition or gender identity or  sexuality acceptance and while i'm going  to talk about this through the lens of  lgbtq  and queer identities and coming out as  such  what i'm going to say actually applies  to basically any time  any creator brings to the attention of  the public something about themselves  that was not known and is in  contradiction to what the assumptions  might have been about them  so as another example if a creator  comes out and begins to talk about  having depression  or anxiety or any number of uh  conditions that affect their day-to-day  lives adhd for the record  um anything like that this sort of same  thing does apply where people will  try and look for signs  and or discuss new meaning  behind things that they did previously  and to a certain extent this is just  going to happen it's not something you  can help  so if for whatever reason you find  yourself looking  at an earlier work before these creators  came  out publicly and you happen to know like  if you're  not scouring it looking for things but  if you're just watching because  maybe it's one you haven't seen before  maybe you felt the need to refresh  yourself on it  your brain is going to start to look for  patterns because that's what human  brains do  that's fine you can't help that i can't  help that  but what you can help and what you need  to be careful of and watch out for  is don't start to take that  attempt for you from your brain to  recognize patterns  don't then make the mistake of trying to  build a narrative of somebody else's  life  absent their input  or consent so there  are some creators out there who have  been  open about the timeline of their own  life and journey of self-discovery heck  i wrote a freaking book about mine  so some of us are fairly public and i  for one have always been pretty open  about answering questions about it  but if they are not like that  if a creator doesn't give you specifics  doesn't give you a timeline doesn't  break it all down for you it's  very invasive to try and do so  anyway to bring up abigail again for a  moment  in her video she the only  frame of time that she gives is one year  and that is the  length of time that she says she has  been out to the people closest to her  in her day-to-day life that gives no  indication  of what her journey was like prior to  that or how long it took  or how many steps there were how long  was the questioning period any number of  things and it's  rude and invasive to try and  assemble that information because if  they wanted you to know  creators would tell you look to a  certain extent  anyone who makes their living on this  platform or anything  vaguely similar to it we are in the  public eye  and we have chosen to make parts of  ourselves  our lives our thoughts our  minds are being public  and visible but  we still have the right to decide what  is going to be public what is going to  be visible  and if we choose not to discuss  something  the best thing that you can do is try  and respect that  and i know some people won't and i know  some people will say well  if you're in the public eye you have no  right to privacy  yeah we do and it's especially  troubling for me when i see people who  believe themselves to be allies and  think that in some way they're  helping or being supportive by going  back and looking for the signs  and like my own inclinations for the  most part is to  not speculate on a creator's personal  life  by and large i mean there's a reason  that i have almost never  in the many years of this channel talked  about a creator's  personal life generally i almost  exclusively talk about their work and  the few times that i  have broadening conversations about  an artist or creator's personal life  i'm honestly kind of terrified to go  back and look at those videos because i  think i  might end up feeling ashamed of them  and part of the reason for my at this  point  increased awareness of this even though  it was something that like i  thought it was pretty good about is i've  made this mistake  there was a point some time ago  when a creator whose work i enjoyed and  still enjoy  i thought that i saw  indications in their videos that  maybe they were like  me little things and  again i'm not going to say any of what  they were  but little things felt familiar  to me little things that were said  little things that were done  made me think i think i know what  they're going through  and then to my  shame and hubris  i reached out to them  basically saying  i think you might be going through  something like this  i've gone through something like this if  you're needing someone to talk to  i'm here and i had no business  doing that i had no right  to speculate about somebody else's  life somebody i didn't know  it was kind of the first time in a while  that i got a reminder  of the fact that i am not immune to  parasocial relationships  the one-sided relationship where you  feel like you know  the person on the screen but they don't  know you  and it was made clear to me that  what i did was invasive  was a violation of their privacy even  though i didn't like i didn't try and  look up stuff i didn't dig through stuff  it was taking in the work that they put  out there but i  still overstepped i'm grateful that i  didn't do so publicly  you know there's no there's no twitter  footprint for this i didn't make a video  about this but i  did still do it  and it was wrong  and having seen  again people who are fans and supportive  start to venture down that road  of  piecing together somebody else's life  story  it begins with oh i want to better  understand them let's look at their old  stuff  oh look at this maybe that was a sign  maybe that was an indicator  and it ends with watching completely  different people  and seeing those people do something and  then leaping to a conclusion of oh  well this other creator did things like  that and  now they've come out as whatever they've  come out as  maybe this other creator who i'm seeing  do these early things  maybe that mean and then suddenly you  are  not only trying to backfill the first  creator's life you are trying to project  forward  a timeline of the life of somebody you  don't  know i have  felt so much joy in my heart in 2021  for abigail for stephanie  for chris and previously for all the  other creators that i've seen come out  before that  but i don't know them i don't know any  of them  and neither do you  and trying to assemble a picture of  their life  that they haven't made public trying to  get a view into their world the kind of  view that they reserve  for their true friends who know them  you have no right it is invasive  it is not supportive and  it's a frighteningly easy thing to slip  into doing  i did i learned from it  so there's that i'll take it  i've seen in too many spaces in too many  areas  people start to head down that same road  it's not good for you to start to think  you know  someone to a level of intimacy that you  don't and can't  and it's not good for them  to have people doing that especially if  they're doing that  in any kind of social forum on twitter  on discords in youtube channels  and again some people will do it in bad  faith  but if you're happy  for someone who's come out  then just take in the information  they are prepared to provide you  please don't speculate about what they  might not be saying  or what dots they haven't connected  if they wanted them connected they would  do it i'm sorry that this was kind of a  down note video especially on a topic  that again  brings me a lot of joy  i feel so wonderful  seeing people with platforms  the size of abigail and chris  and james stephanie sterling the gender  mess  their term i'm allowed to say it  but  and obviously i had my coming out  experiences but  i had it at 10 000 subscribers  they're doing it at hundreds of  thousands  million subscribers  they're doing this the visibility  warms me  and i hope it does you  but don't try and cash that warmth in  to attain something that isn't for you  isn't meant for you they'll give you  what they want you to have  so there we go  sort of how we talk about and process  people who come out and again applicable  to much more than just lgbtq plus  uh people but that's that's my  experience so that's how i'm gonna talk  about it  thank you very much for listening thank  you for your time  and your support this video is made  possible by my  patrons if you wish to support what i do  there's the thing  there are rewards for every tear and all  that sort of thing  i also have merch links other social  medias are down in the description  but you don't have to do any of it  because at the end of the day you are  the council and i'm only running the  meetings  and just remember even if you make  mistakes  like i did you are beautiful  you are valid and you are loved  this council is adjourned  [Music]  hmm  [Applause]  [Music]  hmm  um  [Music]  you
 

